# tally 2.1.8 §4 (#169-e), L §4.4: a window decides a read only where every day agrees. g's day is a window crossing
# the run's end: whether it falls in December, or in January after the run, is open, so flows of konto over either
# month is the window's hole (fa, fb), as h's is over January and February. 2.1.7's refcore counted g nowhere
# (December 0.00). T's fixes/g3/f.
=== m.tally
model pf
  tally 2
  on 2026-03-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source card "invented"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01

place konto: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..
place work: outside lives 1900-01-01..

input wd: date
input wd2: date
input amt: money PLN

move g: transfers
  on wd
  leg cash from work to konto amount amt

move h: transfers
  on wd2
  leg cash from work to konto amount amt

ask fa: flows(konto, 2026-12-01 .. 2026-12-31)
ask fb: flows(konto, 2027-01-01 .. 2027-01-31)
ask fc: flows(konto, 2027-02-01 .. 2027-02-28)
ask be: bal(konto, 2026-12-31)
ask bea: bal(konto, 2027-01-31)
ask few: flows(konto, 2026-12-01 .. 2026-12-31) windows each

version v
  cite card
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  amt = 10.00 PLN "c"
  wd = window(2026-12-20, 2027-01-10) "c"
  wd2 = window(2027-01-25, 2027-02-05) "c"
  opening[konto] = 0.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "own"
=== expect
be: ?"date within window(2026-12-20, 2027-01-10) not precise enough for a balance" (g)
  left out: h, 1 instances, first 2027-01-25
  cut 2026-03-01
bea: ?"after the run's end" (konto)
  cut 2026-03-01
fa: ?"date within window(2026-12-20, 2027-01-10) not precise enough for flows of konto" (g)
  cut 2026-03-01
fb: ?"date within window(2026-12-20, 2027-01-10) not precise enough for flows of konto" (g) ?"date within window(2027-01-25, 2027-02-05) not precise enough for flows of konto" (h)
  cut 2026-03-01
fc: ?"date within window(2027-01-25, 2027-02-05) not precise enough for flows of konto" (h)
  cut 2026-03-01
few [wd = 2026-12-20 .. 2026-12-31]: 10.00 PLN
  cut 2026-03-01
few [wd = 2027-01-01 .. 2027-01-10]: 0.00 PLN
  cut 2026-03-01
